                <pb facs="0521" n="509" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg509"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.2221/403: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Bordeaux</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">George</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bordeaux</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-05-11T17:00:00+01:00">May 11, 1937—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 11—1:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>My May 11, 11 a.m. I am now informed prisoners will be released May 14th with
                    orders to leave France. Further developments will be reported in accordance with
                    Department’s instructions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">George</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
